.IX Title "UDPCLI 1"
.TH UDPCLI 1 2025-11-26 "perl v5.38.2" "BP executables"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
udpcli \- UDP\-based BP convergence layer input task
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBudpcli\fR \fIlocal_hostname\fR[:\fIlocal_port_nbr\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBudpcli\fR is a background "daemon" task that receives UDP datagrams via a
UDP socket bound to \fIlocal_hostname\fR and \fIlocal_port_nbr\fR, extracts
bundles from those datagrams, and passes them to the bundle protocol agent
on the local ION node.
.PP
If not specified, port number defaults to 4556.
.PP
The convergence layer input task is spawned automatically by \fBbpadmin\fR in
response to the 's' (START) command that starts operation of the Bundle
Protocol; the text of the command that is used to spawn the task must be
provided at the time the "udp" convergence layer protocol is added to the BP
database.  The convergence layer input task is terminated by \fBbpadmin\fR
in response to an 'x' (STOP) command.  \fBudpcli\fR can also be spawned and
terminated in response to START and STOP commands that pertain specifically
to the UDP convergence layer protocol.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBudpcli\fR terminated normally, for reasons noted in the \fBion.log\fR file.  If
this termination was not commanded, investigate and solve the problem identified
in the log file and use \fBbpadmin\fR to restart \fBudpcli\fR.
.IP """1""" 4
.IX Item """1"""
\&\fBudpcli\fR terminated abnormally, for reasons noted in the \fBion.log\fR file.
Investigate and solve the problem identified in the log file, then use
\&\fBbpadmin\fR to restart \fBudpcli\fR.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
No configuration files are needed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
The following diagnostics may be issued to the \fBion.log\fR log file:
.IP "udpcli can't attach to BP." 4
.IX Item "udpcli can't attach to BP."
\&\fBbpadmin\fR has not yet initialized Bundle Protocol operations.
.IP "No such udp duct." 4
.IX Item "No such udp duct."
No UDP induct matching \fIlocal_hostname\fR and \fIlocal_port_nbr\fR has been added
to the BP database.  Use \fBbpadmin\fR to stop the UDP convergence-layer
protocol, add the induct, and then restart the UDP protocol.
.IP "CLI task is already started for this duct." 4
.IX Item "CLI task is already started for this duct."
Redundant initiation of \fBudpcli\fR.
.IP "Can't get IP address for host" 4
.IX Item "Can't get IP address for host"
Operating system error.  Check errtext, correct problem, and restart UDP.
.IP "Can't open UDP socket" 4
.IX Item "Can't open UDP socket"
Operating system error.  Check errtext, correct problem, and restart UDP.
.IP "Can't initialize socket" 4
.IX Item "Can't initialize socket"
Operating system error.  Check errtext, correct problem, and restart UDP.
.IP "udpcli can't create receiver thread" 4
.IX Item "udpcli can't create receiver thread"
Operating system error.  Check errtext, correct problem, and restart UDP.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBbpadmin\fR\|(1), \fBbprc\fR\|(5), \fBudpclo\fR\|(1)
